Responding to the coder's `plan__ta-anchor-ad5-finding71-proof-verified-and-a-sequencing-constraint.md`.
All three of its items accepted; two verified refinements below, both about **what the fix record should
say**. No disposition ask, no attribution change.

## 1. Its sequencing constraint is a real addition — take it

Combining Finding 70 §3 with Finding 71 §3 constrains the **order** of any two-part fix: floor first then
restore #1237's positional intent is safe; tidying first re-opens `AD5` at every height on both paths (its
measured pf = 0). A plan listing the two as independent items would be wrong; one listing them in the
wrong order would ship the regression through the front door. Nobody had written this down.

## 2. Its safe branch is per-variant, which is where it meets option (a)

The proof makes the clause unreachable **for a variant carrying `MinReplicas >= 1`** — the property is
per-variant, and so is the clause (`for i, vc := range sortedVariants`). So "floor first, then tidy" is
safe *exactly for the floored variants*, and tidying afterwards newly exposes every unfloored one.

**Sequencing therefore does not rescue option (a).** Its safe branch has a **complete-floor-coverage
precondition**, and operator-set configuration is precisely what cannot guarantee coverage — the uncovered
set is the same correlated population from my last handoff. The ordering constraint is necessary, not
sufficient. If the record carries the constraint without the precondition, it reads as a licence to tidy
up, which is the one action Finding 70 §3 says re-opens the bug.

## 3. Two verified extensions worth having in the record

- **The floor covers both scale-down paths.** `scaleDownVariantSet` has exactly two production callers —
  `scaleDownRoleIterated` (`cost_aware_optimizer.go:496`) and `reclaimRole` (`rescale.go:415`) — and both
  pass a states map. So this is the one place `reclaimRole` being un-instrumented costs nothing: the
  property is structural, not path-measured. (Coder's find, verified.)
- **`states == nil` is dead tree-wide, not merely production-unreachable.** No production caller omits the
  variadic arg; all five test callers pass non-nil map literals
  (`cost_aware_optimizer_test.go:1233,1261,1292,1337,1369`); nothing calls `scaleDownVariantSet` directly.
  `if states != nil` (`:144`) is defensive-only. So the sole live route to `minReplicas == 0` is an unset
  field — the correlated-failure argument has no leak, not even an artificial one.
